| Topic | Resource |
|-------|----------|
| React fundamentals | [React Docs](https://reactjs.org/docs/getting-started.html) |
| Tailwind CSS | [Tailwind Docs](https://tailwindcss.com/docs) |
| Zustand | [Zustand Docs](https://docs.pmnd.rs/zustand) |
| API design | [RESTful API Design](https://restfulapi.net/) |
| Accessibility | [WCAG 2.1](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG21/) |
| Performance | [Lighthouse](https://developers.google.com/web/tools/lighthouse) |
| E2E testing | [Cypress Docs](https://docs.cypress.io/) |

---

## 🎯 Checklist Before Launch

- [ ] All core features implemented and tested
- [ ] Responsive design passes mobile, tablet, desktop
- [ ] Accessibility audit (WCAG 2.1 AA)
- [ ] SEO meta tags, structured data
- [ ] Performance score > 90 in Lighthouse
- [ ] Security hardening (HTTPS, CSP, XSS protection)
- [ ] Analytics & error monitoring set up
- [ ] Backup & rollback plan

---

### Final Thought

Building a frontend for an e‑commerce site is a marathon, not a sprint. Start small, iterate fast, and keep the user at the center of every decision. Once you have a solid foundation, you can add advanced features like AI‑powered recommendations, real‑time inventory, or progressive web app capabilities.

Happy coding! 🚀
